    "created_at": "2015-12-21T21:46:56Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-21T21:46:56Z",
    "body": "I recognize the problem, but I personally at least think it is OK. Strange regexes now become more lenient, allowing some previously-invalid inputs to be submitted. This is not a big issue; client-side validation is in general easy to bypass, so making it more lenient in edge cases is not cause for concern. Nobody's app will fail to load if this change is made.\n\nI think if there is a concern about web authors not figuring out the change, user agents should consider a console log when such SyntaxErrors occur.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
